#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:309
msgid "Metadata and related directives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:311
msgid ""
"Article metadata provides information about the content of an article, such "
"as its context and purpose, and related packages or articles. Adding "
"metadata to an article also improves search engine optimization (SEO) and "
"web indexing. ROS articles also include related directives to manage visible "
"page metadata and article summaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:315
msgid ""
"Every ROS article should include specific metadata and supporting directives "
"so that the documentation renders correctly and related content can be "
"generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:317
msgid "An example of the metadata directive is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:319
msgid ""
".. meta::\n"
"   :contentType: about\n"
"   :experience: beginner\n"
"   :area: contributing, community\n"
"   :distribution: rolling\n"
"   :product: ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:329
msgid "Metadata directive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:331
msgid ""
"Each ROS article must include the ``.. meta::`` directive, and within that, "
"the ``:area:`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:333
msgid ""
"Area metadata is required to enable search filtering and to build lists of "
"related packages or articles. ``:area:`` indicates the area of ROS "
"documentation the article belongs to and its position in the documentation "
"hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:336
msgid ""
"List one or more values, ordered **most specific first**. For example, "
"``:area: contributing, community`` means the article belongs to the "
"``contributing`` subsection inside the ``community`` area. The first value "
"(``contributing``) is the primary value used when building lists of related "
"articles and packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:342
msgid ""
"If the ``:area:`` field is missing, empty, or uses a value outside the "
"allowed vocabulary, the metadata check on the pull request fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:344
msgid ""
"To add a value for the ``:area:`` field, use one or more of the following "
"values. Broader parent areas (such as ``community``, ``framework``, "
"``tools``, and ``capabilities``) may be listed after more specific "
"subsection values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:347
msgid ""
"allowed:\n"
"  - community\n"
"  - contributing\n"
"  - installation\n"
