#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:354
msgid "Optional metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:356
msgid ""
"Some metadata is optional, meaning that omitting it only triggers a warning "
"in the metadata check rather than failing the pull request. It is best "
"practice to include the optional metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:359
msgid ""
"In the ``.. meta::`` directive, the following fields and corresponding "
"values are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:361
msgid "``:contentType:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:362
msgid ""
"The type of content in the article. The value for this field helps structure "
"search results and allows readers to filter content to find the information "
"they need. For a definition of each content type, and help choosing between "
"similar types such as a how-to and a tutorial, see :ref:`Content types "
"<ContentTypes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:366
msgid "Add one of the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:368
msgid "``about``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:369
msgid "``how-to``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:370
msgid "``tutorial``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:371
msgid "``reference``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:372
msgid "``example``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:373
msgid "``learning-path``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:374
msgid "``process-overview``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:375
msgid "``release-note``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:377
msgid "``:experience:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:378
msgid "The level of experience required to understand the article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:380
msgid "Add one or more of the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:382
msgid "``beginner``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:383
msgid "``intermediate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:384
msgid "``expert``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:386
msgid "``:distribution:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:387
msgid "Enables the documentation to work across multiple ROS distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:389
msgid ""
"Always use the ``rolling`` macro as the value. It is replaced with the name "
"of the distribution the documentation is built for, for example ``rolling``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:392
msgid "``:product:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:393
msgid ""
"Identifies the product that the documentation site describes, so that search "
"engines and tools can tell ROS documentation apart from documentation for "
"other projects. It does not refer to individual packages or projects such as "
"Gazebo or RViz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:396
msgid ""
"Always use the ``ROS 2`` macro as the value. It is replaced with the product "
"name, ``ROS 2``, which is defined in ``conf.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:400
msgid "Show metadata directive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:402
msgid ""
"Each ROS article should include the ``.. showmeta::`` directive to manage "
"the visible page metadata. Omitting it triggers a warning in the metadata "
"check rather than failing the pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:405
msgid ""
"``.. showmeta::`` renders the specified metadata at the top of a published "
"article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:407
msgid "Add the following related directive to your article:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:409
msgid ""
".. showmeta::\n"
"   :order: area, contentType, experience\n"
"   :labels: area=Area, contentType=Content type, experience=Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:416
msgid "Short description directive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:418
msgid ""
"Each ROS article should include the ``.. short-description::`` directive. "
"Omitting it triggers a warning in the metadata check rather than failing the "
"pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:421
msgid ""
"``.. short-description::`` provides a two or three sentence explanation "
"about the article's content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:423
msgid ""
"Use the following structure to create a short description, making sure your "
"sentences answer each of the questions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:425
msgid ""
"Sentence 1 - Context: Why would a user be interested in reading this article?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:427
msgid ""
"Sentence 2 - Purpose: What does the article describe or what will a user get "
"out of reading it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:429
msgid ""
"Sentence 3 - Outcome: What will the user be able to do after reading the "
"article or following the guidance? For ``about`` type articles, this "
"sentence is optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:432
msgid "You can use the following examples to guide you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:434
msgid "Short description for :doc:`About ROS<../../../About-ROS>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:436
msgid ""
".. short-description::\n"
"   ROS (Robot Operating System) is an open-source ecosystem that provides "
"the framework, tools, and libraries for building, deploying, running, and "
"maintaining robotic applications.\n"
"   This article introduces the main areas of the ecosystem and outlines "
"their intended use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:442
msgid ""
"Short description for :doc:`Using the Node Interfaces Template Class (C++) — "
"tutorial<../../../ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Using-Node-"
"Interfaces-Template-Class>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:444
msgid ""
".. short-description::\n"
"   Different ROS node types can expose the same capabilities through "
"different C++ classes.\n"
"   This tutorial explains how to use "
"``rclcpp::node_interfaces::NodeInterfaces<>`` to write functions that accept "
"both standard and lifecycle nodes.\n"
"   After completing it, you can pass node interfaces compactly and retrieve "
"node information reliably."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:452
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:620
msgid "Related content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:454
msgid ""
"Related content is the packages or articles linked from an article based on "
"the primary (first) value in the ``:area:`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:456
msgid ""
"To generate related articles automatically at build time, add the ``.. ros-"
"related-articles::`` directive. Write a short intro line such as ``Related "
"articles:`` above it. Matching uses the primary ``:area:`` value: other "
"pages that include that value anywhere in their own ``:area:`` list are "
"listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:460
msgid ""
"Related articles:\n"
"\n"
".. ros-related-articles::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:466
msgid ""
"To generate related packages in the browser from the rosdistro cache, add "
"the ``.. ros-related-packages::`` directive. Write a short intro line such "
"as ``Related packages:`` above it. Matching uses the primary ``:area:`` "
"value against each package's ``<ros2_documentation_area>`` export in "
"``package.xml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:470
msgid ""
"Related packages:\n"
"\n"
".. ros-related-packages::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:476
msgid ""
"You can also add related content manually. Use the following formatting and "
"naming conventions. You can check :doc:`About client libraries <../../../ROS-"
"Framework/About-Client-Libraries>` for an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:480
msgid ""
"Related content\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"Related articles\n"
"^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"\n"
"* Related article here\n"
"\n"
"Related packages\n"
"^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"\n"
"Core ROS packages\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"* Package here\n"
"\n"
"Community packages\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"* Package here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:504
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:506
msgid ""
"There are two types of directives used for generating a table of contents: "
"``.. toctree::`` and ``.. contents::``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:508
msgid ""
"The ``.. toctree::`` directive is used in top-level pages, for "
"example, :doc:`Community <../../../The-ROS2-Project>`, to organize and "
"display the list of subarticles. This directive creates both the left-hand "
"navigation pane and the in-page navigation links to the subarticles. It "
"helps readers understand the structure of the documentation sections and "
"navigate between articles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:512
msgid ""
".. toctree::\n"
"   :maxdepth: 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:517
msgid ""
"The ``.. contents::`` directive is used for generating the table of contents "
"for a particular article by parsing all headings in the article. The table "
"of contents shows readers the structural overview of the content and helps "
"them navigate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:520
msgid ""
"The ``.. contents::`` directive defines the maximum depth of sections "
"displayed in the article's table of contents. The recommended value is "
"``:depth: 2`` to ensure only section and subsection headings are displayed. "
"This is particularly important for large articles with many nested sections, "
"for example, :doc:`Quality Guide <../Contributing-to-code/Quality-Guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:524
msgid ""
".. contents:: Contents\n"
"   :depth: 2\n"
"   :local:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:533
msgid "Content types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:535
msgid ""
"Content types define patterns in the content of different types of articles. "
"They are designed to meet a range of information needs. The main purpose of "
"content types is to set expectations for humans and AI about the expected "
"content range and scope. The patterns defined by content types are also "
"valuable for enabling efficient content creation and maintenance. To best "
"support information retrieval by both humans and machines, each article "
"contains a single content type."
msgstr ""

