#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:631
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:633
msgid ""
"What metadata and directives are required in a ROS documentation article?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:634
msgid ""
"Every ROS article must include a ``.. meta::`` directive with an ``:area:`` "
"field. List ``:area:`` values most specific first; the first value is the "
"primary value used for related content. Each article should also include the "
"``.. showmeta::`` and ``.. short-description::`` directives. A missing, "
"empty, or disallowed ``:area:`` value causes the metadata check on the pull "
"request to fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:639
msgid ""
"How should I format sentences and white space in a ROS reStructuredText file?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:640
msgid ""
"Write only one sentence per line to make the file easier to review and "
"modify. Do not leave trailing white space, because the ROS documentation "
"linter will not accept pull requests that contain it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:643
msgid "When should I use bash instead of console for a code block?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:644
msgid ""
"Use bash for commands or content intended to be copied into a script file. "
"Use console for commands that readers should run in a terminal, especially "
"when you also need to show terminal output. In console blocks, prefix "
"command lines with ``$`` so the copy button copies commands rather than "
"output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:648
msgid "When should I use ``:doc:`` and ``:ref:`` for internal links?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines.rst:649
msgid ""
"Use ``:doc:`` to link to another article in the ROS documentation, using its "
"relative path. Use ``:ref:`` to link to a defined target such as a heading, "
"image, or code section in the same article or another article."
msgstr ""
